    "result_text": "The test suite consists solely of `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are helper base/support classes with no `@Test` methods). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule: **`SILVER`** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **`BRONZE`**.\n\nThe owner response DTO is generated from OpenAPI and populated via MapStruct, following the existing derived-field pattern (`membershipNumber`, `displayName`, `initials`). Two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` plus a `membershipTier(owner)` helper returning `\"SILVER\"` when the owner has no namesakes (`namesakeCount == 0`) and a non-blank email, else `\"BRONZE\"` (null-safe on both fields for legacy/seed owners).\n\nSince `membershipTier` is derived at response time from the persisted `namesakeCount` and `email`, no pipeline/YAML step changes were needed.\n\nResults: `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` both pass; full suite: **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
